{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-6-1","title":"Job 6:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job shews that his complaints are not causeless. 8 He wishes for death, wherein he is assured of comfort. 14 He reproves his friends of unkindness.</p>\n<p>answered. 4:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-2","title":"Job 6:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>throughly. 4:5; 23:2 laid. Heb. lifted up.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-3","title":"Job 6:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>heavier. Pr 27:3; Mt 11:28 my words are swallowed up. that is, I want words to expressmy grief. 37:19,20; Ps 40:5; 77:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-4","title":"Job 6:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the arrows. 16:12-14; De 32:23,42; Ps 7:13; 18:14; 21:12; 38:2; 45:5; La 3:12,13 drinketh up. De 32:24; Ps 143:7; Pr 18:14; Mr 14:33,34; 15:34 the terrors. 9:17; 30:15; 31:23; Ps 88:15,16; 2Co 5:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-5","title":"Job 6:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>when he hath grass. Heb. at grass. Ps 104:14 loweth. Ps 42:1; Jer 14:6; Joe 1:18-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-6","title":"Job 6:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>that which. 25; 16:2; Le 2:13; Lu 14:34; Col 4:6 taste. 30; 12:11; 34:3; Ps 119:103; Heb 6:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-7","title":"Job 6:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>as my sorrowful meat. 1Ki 17:12; 22:27; Ps 102:9; Eze 4:14,16; 12:18,19; Da 10:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-8","title":"Job 6:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>the thing that I long for. Heb. my expectation. 11-13; 17:14-16; Ps 119:81</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-9","title":"Job 6:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>that it would. 3:20-22; 7:15,16; 14:13; Nu 11:14,15; 1Ki 19:4; Jon 4:3,8; Re 9:6 that he would. 19:21; Ps 32:4; Isa 48:10-13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-10","title":"Job 6:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Then. 3:22; 21:33 I would. 9:4 let him not. De 29:20; Ro 8:32; 2Pe 2:4,5 have not concealed. 23:12; Ps 37:30; 40:9,10; 71:17,18; 119:13; Ac 20:20,27 the Holy One. Le 19:2; 1Sa 2:2; Isa 30:11,12; 57:15; Ho 11:9; Hab 1:12; 3:3 Re 3:7; 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-11","title":"Job 6:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>What. 7:5-7; 10:20; 13:25,28; 17:1,14-16; Ps 39:5; 90:5-10; 102:23 Ps 103:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-12","title":"Job 6:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>of brass. Heb. brasen. 40:18; 41:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-13","title":"Job 6:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Is not my. 19:28; 2Co 1:12; Ga 6:4 and is wisdom. 12:2,3; 13:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-14","title":"Job 6:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>To him. 4:3,4; 16:5; 19:21; Pr 17:17; Ro 12:15; 1Co 12:26; 2Co 11:29; Ga 6:2 Heb 13:3 is afflicted. Heb. melteth. he forsaketh. Ge 20:11; Ps 36:1-3; Lu 23:40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-15","title":"Job 6:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>My brethren. 19:19; Ps 38:11; 41:9; 55:12-14; 88:18; Jer 9:4,5; 30:14; Mic 7:5,6 Joh 13:18; 16:32 as the stream. Jer 15:18; Jude 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-17","title":"Job 6:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>vanish. Heb. are cut off. when it is hot they are consumed.Heb. in the heat thereof they are extinguished. 1Ki 17:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-19","title":"Job 6:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Tema. Ge 25:15; Isa 21:14; Jer 25:23 Sheba. Ge 10:7; 25:3; 1Ki 10:1; Ps 72:10; Eze 27:22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-20","title":"Job 6:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>confounded. Jer 14:3,4; 17:13; Ro 5:5; 9:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-21","title":"Job 6:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>ye are nothing. or, ye are like to them. Heb. to it. 15; 13:4; Ps 62:9; Isa 2:22; Jer 17:5,6 nothing. Heb. not. ye see. 2:11-13; Ps 38:11; Pr 19:7; Jer 51:9; Mt 26:31,56; 2Ti 4:16 Re 18:9,10,17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-22","title":"Job 6:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Bring unto me. 42:11; 1Sa 12:3; Ac 20:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-23","title":"Job 6:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Redeem. 5:20; Le 25:48; Ne 5:8; Ps 49:7,8,15; 107:2; Jer 15:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-24","title":"Job 6:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Teach me. 5:27; 32:11,15,16; 33:1,31-33; 34:32; Ps 32:8; Pr 9:9; 25:12 Jas 1:19 I will. Ps 39:1,2; Jas 3:2 cause me. 10:2; Ps 19:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-25","title":"Job 6:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>forcible. 4:4; 16:5; Pr 12:18; 16:21-24; 18:21; 25:11; Ec 12:10,11 what doth. 13:5; 16:3,4; 21:34; 24:25; 32:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-26","title":"Job 6:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>reprove. 2:10; 3:3-26; 4:3,4; 34:3-9; 38:2; 40:5,8; 42:3,7; Mt 12:37 one that. 4,9; 10:1 as wind. 8:2; Ho 12:1; Eph 4:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-27","title":"Job 6:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>overwhelm. Heb. cause to fall upon. the fatherless. 22:9; 24:3,9; 29:12; 31:17,21; Ex 22:22-24; Ps 82:3; Pr 23:10,11 Eze 22:7; Mal 3:5; Jas 1:27 ye dig. Ps 7:15; 57:6; Jer 18:20,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-28","title":"Job 6:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>evident unto you. Heb. before your face. if I lie. 11:3; 13:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-29","title":"Job 6:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>Return. 17:10; Mal 3:18 my righteousness. 27:4-6 in it. that is, in this matter.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-6-30","title":"Job 6:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>iniquity. 33:8-12; 42:3-6 cannot. 6; 12:11; 34:3; Heb 5:14 taste. Heb. palate.</p>"}]}